# Design Decisions

## Wallet Ledger

Instead of updating balances directly, every operation creates a transaction record.

Advantages

- audit trail
- rollback support
- reconciliation
- history

---

## Transactions

All wallet operations run inside

```
db.transaction(...)
```

This guarantees

- atomicity

If one query fails

everything rolls back.

---

## Row Locking

Transfers use

```
SELECT ... FOR UPDATE
```

to prevent concurrent balance modifications.

This avoids race conditions.

---

## Password Security

Passwords are hashed using bcrypt.

Plain passwords are never stored.

---

## Authentication

JWT-based authentication.

Every protected endpoint requires

```
Authorization

Bearer <token>
```

---

## Validation

Every endpoint validates input using Zod before reaching business logic.

---

# API Documentation

## Register

POST

```
/api/v1/users/register
```

Request

```json
{
  "first_name":"John",
  "last_name":"Doe",
  "email":"john@test.com",
  "phone_number":"08011111111",
  "password":"Password123!"
}
```

---

## Login

POST

```
/api/v1/users/login
```

---

## Profile

GET

```
/api/v1/users/me
```

---

## Fund Wallet

POST

```
/api/v1/transactions/fund
```

---

## Withdraw

POST

```
/api/v1/transactions/withdraw
```

---

## Transfer

POST

```
/api/v1/transactions/transfer
```

---

## Transaction History

GET

```
/api/v1/transactions?page=1&limit=10
```

